<title>USA: Idaho Power sees abundant 1997 hydropower.</title>
<headline>Idaho Power sees abundant 1997 hydropower.</headline>
<dateline>BOISE, Idaho 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Idaho Power Co said Tuesday it expects favorable hydroelectric generating conditions throughout 1997.</p>
<p>With streamflows above average, the company estimates that 56 percent of its 1997 energy requirements will come from its hydro operations, 27 percent from thermal operations and 17 percent purchased power and other interchanges.</p>
<p>In 1996, Idaho Power sold 17,306 gigawatt hours of electricity.</p>
</text>
